00:31:22,299 --> 00:31:25,802
Well, if she can't come to the
phone, take the fucking phone to her.

496
00:31:25,886 --> 00:31:28,222
- Ah, you went for ten after all.
- Yeah.

497
00:31:28,222 --> 00:31:30,098
The message is,

498
00:31:30,182 --> 00:31:34,269
"Call me urgently. I have
the results of your test."

499
00:31:34,353 --> 00:31:36,980
Makes up for River leaving
early without a purchase.

500
00:31:37,064 --> 00:31:38,899
Yeah. Uh, just get
her to fucking call me.

501
00:31:39,900 --> 00:31:42,236
Uh, when exactly did Cartwright leave?

502
00:31:42,903 --> 00:31:46,323
I don't know exactly.
About two hours ago?

503
00:31:46,323 --> 00:31:47,533
Just before Sid.

504
00:31:47,533 --> 00:31:50,077
All right. Well, fuck off.

505
00:32:04,591 --> 00:32:06,218
Jesus, this time tomorrow morning.

506
00:32:07,094 --> 00:32:09,054
Yeah, we'll be back here.

507
00:32:09,054 --> 00:32:13,058
Same shit, different...
You... You mean the hostage.

508
00:32:13,058 --> 00:32:15,175
Of course, um, well, the... the...

509
00:32:15,176 --> 00:32:16,353
they'll find him
before then, won't they?

510
00:32:16,353 --> 00:32:17,980
I mean, they have to.

511
00:32:17,980 --> 00:32:19,356
Yeah, let's hope so.

512
00:32:20,858 --> 00:32:22,568
You doing anything tonight?

513
00:32:22,568 --> 00:32:24,945
I'm praying for a lottery win.

514
00:32:25,696 --> 00:32:28,740
But I mean, that's not, you know,
necessarily location specific.

515
00:32:28,824 --> 00:32:30,784
I... I could do that on... on the move.

516
00:32:31,410 --> 00:32:35,497
Hey, you two flakies. You
forgetting we have a date tonight?

517
00:32:37,541 --> 00:32:40,752
Shit. Sorry, Struan,
um, I've double-booked.

518
00:32:40,836 --> 00:32:42,796
I'm meeting a friend tonight now. Sorry.

519
00:32:42,880 --> 00:32:47,092
You met a friend last night too.
It's good to be popular. Min?

520
00:32:47,968 --> 00:32:50,220
Clare's texted. Her
sister's having a mare.

521
00:32:50,304 --> 00:32:52,306
Um, splitting up with her boyfriend.

522
00:32:52,306 --> 00:32:55,309
So, yeah, I'm on
full-on dad duty tonight.

523
00:32:56,268 --> 00:33:00,189
Very well. We had such a laugh
last time we went for a drink.

524
00:33:00,689 --> 00:33:02,316
We must do it again at some point.

525
00:33:02,316 --> 00:33:03,400
Oh, absolutely.

526
00:33:03,400 --> 00:33:04,776
Let's do Christmas drinks.

527
00:33:05,360 --> 00:33:06,570
It's February.

528
00:33:42,397 --> 00:33:43,815
What the hell are you doing here?

529
00:33:43,899 --> 00:33:45,150
I could ask you the same thing.

530
00:33:45,734 --> 00:33:46,902
Thought you might want a coffee.

531
00:33:46,902 --> 00:33:48,445
You didn't have any in the café.

532
00:33:49,696 --> 00:33:51,073
Sorry, have you been following me?

533
00:33:51,573 --> 00:33:52,950
You'd better hope not.

534
00:33:52,950 --> 00:33:54,080
Because that'd mean I tracked you

535
00:33:54,081 --> 00:33:55,369
halfway across London
without you noticing.

536
00:33:55,369 --> 00:33:57,287
- Ah, Jesus Christ.
- I thought you were good at this.

537
00:33:57,371 --> 00:34:00,541
Maybe that story about you
tailing Taverner is just a myth.

538
00:34:00,541 --> 00:34:01,725
That... Uh, no.

539
00:34:01,726 --> 00:34:03,877
Not a myth, actually.
That really did happen.

540
00:34:03,961 --> 00:34:05,128
Mmm.

541
00:34:08,432 --> 00:34:09,450
I was assigned to follow

542
00:34:09,451 --> 00:34:12,844
the Shadow Minister for
Education as an exercise.

543
00:34:12,928 --> 00:34:14,638
But then he had a heart
attack the night before.

544
00:34:14,638 --> 00:34:17,641
So I followed Taverner instead.

545
00:34:17,641 --> 00:34:20,018
And I watched her do
everything. Everything.

546
00:34:20,018 --> 00:34:23,647
Gym, breakfast, office,
gym again at lunch.

547
00:34:24,606 --> 00:34:26,567
I got within 10 feet and she never knew.

548
00:34:27,150 --> 00:34:30,737
Well, not until I showed her
the photographs the next day.

549
00:34:30,821 --> 00:34:32,864
And that bit about her applauding you?

550
00:34:33,614 --> 00:34:35,236
People have made more of
that than it warranted.

551
00:34:35,237 --> 00:34:36,410
It was just three claps.

552
00:34:36,493 --> 00:34:38,290
You should be applauding
me. I kept an eye on Hobden

553
00:34:38,291 --> 00:34:39,371
while you went to get your car.

554
00:34:39,371 --> 00:34:40,539
I should be applau...

555
00:34:41,623 --> 00:34:43,833
I would have stuck out,
standing around on the street.

556
00:34:43,917 --> 00:34:44,960
Well, I didn't.

557
00:34:44,960 --> 00:34:48,338
But then, as we've established, I
am better at surveillance than you.

558
00:34:48,422 --> 00:34:51,216
That's just... Depends
how you look at it.

559
00:34:51,717 --> 00:34:52,717
Come on.

560
00:34:53,510 --> 00:34:54,844
Unbelievable.

561
00:34:54,928 --> 00:34:57,556
You love it when I'm hard on you.

562
00:35:00,601 --> 00:35:03,812
So, what did you find in Hobden's
rubbish that put you in spy mode?

563
00:35:05,439 --> 00:35:08,984
Ho predicted that Hobden would've
made something called a thermite pot,

564
00:35:09,943 --> 00:35:12,905
which is basically a geek way
for the clinically paranoid

565
00:35:12,905 --> 00:35:14,364
to burn the computer to ash.

566
00:35:14,865 --> 00:35:19,620
And I found some steel wool and
rusting coffee filters in his rubbish.

567
00:35:20,204 --> 00:35:23,957
He'd been making iron oxide. It's
one of the ingredients for thermite.

568
00:35:24,541 --> 00:35:25,918
So he's got something on his hard drive

569
00:35:25,918 --> 00:35:28,337
- he doesn't want anyone to find?
- Mmm.

570
00:35:31,298 --> 00:35:32,299
That is disgusting.

571
00:35:32,299 --> 00:35:33,967
That'd be the arsenic.

572
00:35:35,636 --> 00:35:36,636
How'd you get Ho to help?

573
00:35:38,847 --> 00:35:40,974
I promised I'd tell him
why he's in Slough House.

574
00:35:41,058 --> 00:35:44,186
- Do you know?
- I do, yeah. Do you?

575
00:35:44,186 --> 00:35:45,395
Mm-hmm.

576
00:35:45,479 --> 00:35:47,648
Well, anyway, uh, he
couldn't do what I asked him,

577
00:35:47,648 --> 00:35:50,317
which was to hack into Hobden's
email, so I didn't have to tell him.

578
00:35:50,901 --> 00:35:51,944
Would you have told him?

579
00:35:51,944 --> 00:35:53,612
Yeah, he wants to know.

580
00:35:53,612 --> 00:35:56,198
- How would you have told him?
- I don't know. With words.

581
00:35:57,282 --> 00:36:01,078
Okay. Pretend I'm Roddy Ho,
and you tell me that the reason

582
00:36:01,078 --> 00:36:02,605
I've been shipped out to Slough House

583
00:36:02,606 --> 00:36:04,915
is because I'm an insufferable prick.

584
00:36:04,915 --> 00:36:06,083
- I got moved...
- I'd sugarcoat it.

585
00:36:06,083 --> 00:36:07,915
from every department
I worked in in MI5

586
00:36:07,916 --> 00:36:09,461
and Slough House was
the only place left.

587
00:36:09,545 --> 00:36:11,088
But if he had gotten
me into Hobden's emails,

588
00:36:11,088 --> 00:36:13,215
- can we agree that would've been useful?
- That...

589
00:36:13,215 --> 00:36:14,967
He once put someone on
the sex offenders register

590
00:36:14,967 --> 00:36:16,593
because they nicked his seat on a bus.

591
00:36:16,677 --> 00:36:17,719
I didn't have to tell him.

592
00:36:17,803 --> 00:36:19,930
- Imagine what he'd do to you.
- So why are we arguing about this?

593
00:36:23,016 --> 00:36:27,020
Do you think Roddy could find
out why Lamb is in Slough House?

594
00:36:27,104 --> 00:36:29,356
No. Otherwise he
would've already done it.

595
00:36:29,982 --> 00:36:31,733
Hmm.

596
00:36:40,659 --> 00:36:44,496
Why are you here, Sid? Not
in the car, at Slough House.

597
00:36:44,580 --> 00:36:46,540
I thought Slough House was like prison.

598
00:36:46,540 --> 00:36:49,459
You're not supposed to
ask what you're in for.

599
00:36:49,960 --> 00:36:51,295
Well, you know why I'm there.

600
00:36:52,045 --> 00:36:54,131
Yeah, but everybody
knows why you're there.

601
00:36:55,382 --> 00:36:57,467
I was gonna give you a compliment,
but you can shove it now.

602
00:36:57,551 --> 00:36:59,678
Suit yourself. I get
enough flattery from Lamb.

603
00:36:59,678 --> 00:37:01,430
But that's what I mean.

604
00:37:03,682 --> 00:37:05,684
He can see that you're
not like the others.

605
00:37:06,435 --> 00:37:07,853
Because you're not.

606
00:37:09,146 --> 00:37:11,523
I mean, Min,

607
00:37:12,065 --> 00:37:13,066
Struan,

608
00:37:14,026 --> 00:37:15,027
Roddy,

609
00:37:16,028 --> 00:37:18,805
maybe not Louisa, but definitely Moody,

610
00:37:18,806 --> 00:37:19,990
they were always headed for the skids.

611
00:37:19,990 --> 00:37:21,450
They're useless, but you're...

612
00:37:22,826 --> 00:37:24,870
You know, it just doesn't make sense.

613
00:37:27,039 --> 00:37:29,875
But, um, whatever the reason
for being put in Slough House,

614
00:37:29,875 --> 00:37:33,086
it must've... must've
come out of nowhere, right?

615
00:37:36,298 --> 00:37:37,299
Yeah.

616
00:37:38,884 --> 00:37:40,469
Yeah, it did, and it's just...

617
00:37:42,304 --> 00:37:43,972
just none of your business.

618
00:37:45,641 --> 00:37:46,642
Okay.

619
00:37:48,268 --> 00:37:50,938
- So how long are you gonna sit here for?
- Just until Hobden goes to sleep.

620
00:37:52,147 --> 00:37:53,524
Then I'm gonna go in there and find out

621
00:37:53,524 --> 00:37:56,026
what's on that laptop he's
been carrying around all day.

622
00:38:32,020 --> 00:38:33,397
- Hiya.
- You all right, love?

623
00:38:33,397 --> 00:38:36,525
- Yeah, can I get a vodka soda, please?
- Yep, ice and slice?

624
00:38:36,525 --> 00:38:37,609
Yes, please.

625
00:38:41,029 --> 00:38:42,739
I'm just gonna be round there.

626
00:38:43,907 --> 00:38:45,158
All right.

627
00:38:49,162 --> 00:38:50,747
Thought you were babysitting.

628
00:38:52,833 --> 00:38:54,334
Thought you were meeting a friend.

629
00:38:55,836 --> 00:38:57,087
Poor Struan.

630
00:38:58,088 --> 00:39:00,132
Yeah, if he saw us
here, I think he'd cry.

631
00:39:00,716 --> 00:39:01,967
You're not going home, then?

632
00:39:02,676 --> 00:39:05,596
Uh, well, no. I thought I'd just
decompress a bit first, you know.

633
00:39:05,596 --> 00:39:06,930
Yeah. Fair enough.

634
00:39:07,014 --> 00:39:10,684
It's been, uh, one hell of
a day protecting the nation.

635
00:39:11,351 --> 00:39:13,896
Imagine the consequences if
I didn't turn up for work, eh?

636
00:39:13,896 --> 00:39:15,105
Thanks.

637
00:39:15,189 --> 00:39:17,774
Well, then I'd be left alone with
Struan. So please keep showing up.

638
00:39:17,858 --> 00:39:19,610
You should get danger money for that.

639
00:39:23,071 --> 00:39:24,390
So I'm assuming you didn't have

640
00:39:24,391 --> 00:39:26,366
a friend around last night either, then?

641
00:39:26,450 --> 00:39:27,451
Mm-mmm.

642
00:39:30,454 --> 00:39:32,372
You know, I don't
actually have any friends.

643
00:39:34,708 --> 00:39:37,628
No, I mean that I have, uh...

644
00:39:37,628 --> 00:39:39,004
I have people that I know,

645
00:39:39,004 --> 00:39:41,548
but, like, no one that I can talk to.

646
00:39:41,632 --> 00:39:43,592
Not... Not about work anyway.

647
00:39:44,635 --> 00:39:47,054
Do you not stay in touch with any
of your old colleagues from the Park?

648
00:39:47,054 --> 00:39:49,890
Mm-mmm. No, they kinda shunned me.

649
00:39:50,641 --> 00:39:52,059
Well, I wasn't just shunned.

650
00:39:52,059 --> 00:39:55,979
I was shamed by everyone

651
00:39:56,063 --> 00:39:58,565
after... you know.

652
00:39:58,649 --> 00:40:00,400
You left a top secret file on a train.

653
00:40:00,484 --> 00:40:01,902
Yes.

654
00:40:01,902 --> 00:40:03,237
That.

655
00:40:09,785 --> 00:40:13,455
I was shaving in the bathroom,
listening to the radio,

656
00:40:13,539 --> 00:40:15,040
when it hit the headlines that...

657
00:40:15,999 --> 00:40:18,544
well, the file had been found
by a member of the public.

658
00:40:19,962 --> 00:40:24,132
And, uh, Clare just said,
"What fool did that?"

659
00:40:26,218 --> 00:40:28,053
And I just started crying.

660
00:40:29,596 --> 00:40:31,598
Uh, I thought maybe she'd hug me.

661
00:40:31,682 --> 00:40:33,559
But nah. She didn't.

662
00:40:33,559 --> 00:40:35,519
She just said...

663
00:40:36,144 --> 00:40:37,729
"Min, you fucking idiot."

664
00:40:37,813 --> 00:40:39,690
Wow. That's, um...

665
00:40:42,442 --> 00:40:43,569
And, uh,

666
00:40:43,569 --> 00:40:46,822
- are things okay now between you two?
- Oh, God, yeah. I'm getting divorced.

667
00:40:49,658 --> 00:40:51,869
I guess she saw me
differently after that.

668
00:40:54,621 --> 00:40:56,248
And you let us all think
you had a home life.

669
00:40:56,248 --> 00:40:57,920
Well, yeah. I mean,

670
00:40:57,921 --> 00:41:00,919
I keep up the lie partly because
I don't want to accept it.

671
00:41:01,003 --> 00:41:03,964
Partly because I do not
wanna give Lamb any more ammo.

672
00:41:04,840 --> 00:41:06,925
And, well, perhaps most importantly,

673
00:41:07,009 --> 00:41:09,428
because it stops me having
to go to the pub with Struan.

674
00:41:09,428 --> 00:41:12,139
I mean, oh, my God.

675
00:41:12,139 --> 00:41:14,183
Oh.

676
00:41:14,183 --> 00:41:16,560
- He makes me yearn for Alan Black.
- Yeah.

677
00:41:16,560 --> 00:41:19,188
Black was like Struan with depression,
but at least he didn't, you know,

678
00:41:19,188 --> 00:41:21,106
wanna try and continue
talking after work.

679
00:41:21,190 --> 00:41:23,192
He's just so freaking keen. He's like...

680
00:41:23,192 --> 00:41:25,527
- Yeah.
- ... you know, "Let's do a monthly dinner."

681
00:41:25,611 --> 00:41:26,987
"Let's go paintballing."Let's... "

682
00:41:26,987 --> 00:41:29,823
So I guess we'd say to
those who have taken him...

683
00:41:29,907 --> 00:41:33,994
Please, he's done no harm to
you. Just... Just let him go.

684
00:41:35,287 --> 00:41:36,496
The police are now saying

685
00:41:36,580 --> 00:41:38,749
the threat to Leeds
University student Hassan...

686
00:42:05,526 --> 00:42:06,902
Get me Ho.

687
00:42:09,029 --> 00:42:10,489
I think he's gone.

688
00:42:12,032 --> 00:42:13,659
Then get him back.

689
00:43:43,207 --> 00:43:44,958
Who was Hobden trying to call?

690
00:43:45,042 --> 00:43:48,629
Just a bunch of right-leaning
editors and journalists,

691
00:43:49,254 --> 00:43:51,173
but none of them took his calls.

692
00:43:52,257 --> 00:43:54,426
But he rang Peter Judd seven times.

693
00:43:54,510 --> 00:43:56,595
Ugh, Judd is the worst.

694
00:43:58,013 --> 00:43:59,223
Yeah.

695
00:44:05,687 --> 00:44:07,481
Hello?

696
00:44:09,066 --> 00:44:10,609
I... I can't talk at the moment.

697
00:44:12,319 --> 00:44:14,488
- No, I'm watching him right now.
- Update me later.

698
00:44:14,488 --> 00:44:16,573
I will, but I have... I have to go.

699
00:44:16,657 --> 00:44:18,075
Okay.

700
00:44:19,993 --> 00:44:21,495
Who's Aunt Zadie?

701
00:44:23,413 --> 00:44:24,414
Um...

702
00:44:27,626 --> 00:44:28,627
There is no Aunt Zadie.

703
00:44:28,627 --> 00:44:31,672
I put that in so if
anyone got into my phone,

704
00:44:31,672 --> 00:44:33,298
they wouldn't know who
I'd been talking to.

705
00:44:33,382 --> 00:44:34,842
Wait, well, who were
you talking to then?

706
00:44:35,634 --> 00:44:37,386
Someone who knows you're
watching Robert Hobden?

707
00:44:38,554 --> 00:44:39,555
That's not what I said.

708
00:44:40,180 --> 00:44:42,307
Yes, you did. You just
said, "I'm watching him now."

709
00:44:42,391 --> 00:44:45,727
Listen... There's a reason I didn't
tell you why I'm in Slough House.

710
00:44:45,811 --> 00:44:47,300
No, no, no. Sid...

711
00:44:47,301 --> 00:44:49,648
really, seriously, you
don't have to tell me why.

712
00:44:49,648 --> 00:44:51,612
It's not for something
you did in the field,

713
00:44:51,613 --> 00:44:53,318
because you're a brilliant agent.

714
00:44:54,653 --> 00:44:55,779
Kind-of-brilliant agent.

715
00:44:55,863 --> 00:44:58,115
So it's obviously something
to do with your personal life,

716
00:44:58,115 --> 00:45:00,826
- which is none of my business.
- No. River, it is your business. I...

717
00:45:03,120 --> 00:45:04,830
I didn't just follow you here today.

718
00:45:07,165 --> 00:45:08,375
That was Taverner,

719
00:45:09,209 --> 00:45:10,836
and I wasn't telling her
I was watching Hobden.

720
00:45:10,836 --> 00:45:12,880
I was telling her I was watching you.

721
00:45:18,093 --> 00:45:19,094
Are you being serious?

722
00:45:21,305 --> 00:45:23,348
You're watching me for Taverner?

723
00:45:23,891 --> 00:45:24,892
Wha...

724
00:45:26,185 --> 00:45:27,728
Why would she want you watching me?

725
00:45:27,728 --> 00:45:29,777
Look, I don't know,
but it's the reason why

726
00:45:29,778 --> 00:45:31,148
I've been sent to Slough House.

727
00:45:31,148 --> 00:45:33,150
To... To... To keep an eye on you.

728
00:45:35,777 --> 00:45:36,778
You're kidding, right?

729
00:45:38,530 --> 00:45:39,698
No.

730
00:45:40,866 --> 00:45:42,868
No, I'm not. I'm... Uh.

731
00:45:46,622 --> 00:45:47,831
Shit.

732
00:45:49,666 --> 00:45:50,834
Shit. Look.

733
00:45:53,378 --> 00:45:55,047
I'll cover the front.

734
00:46:19,488 --> 00:46:20,864
Stop it!

735
00:46:23,825 --> 00:46:25,577
Please. Please.

736
00:46:28,789 --> 00:46:32,459
Get him off me. Get him off me!

737
00:46:33,585 --> 00:46:34,795
Listen to me.

738
00:46:34,795 --> 00:46:37,506
Let him go and put the gun down.
Armed response are two minutes out.

739
00:46:37,506 --> 00:46:40,133
If they see you with a gun,
they're just gonna kill you.

740
00:46:40,759 --> 00:46:42,302
- Did you hear me?
- What do you want?

741
00:46:42,386 --> 00:46:43,637
Put the gun down.

742
00:47:00,737 --> 00:47:02,739
Sid.

